meta {
  name: List Overdue Tickets
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/management-dashboard/alerts/overdue-tickets?range=ytd
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  range: ytd
  ~page: 1
  ~pageSize: 50
  ~producerIds:
  ~leadSourceIds: {{mailerLeadSourceId}}
  ~policyTypes: Auto
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{managementDashboardToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the total is the card's number", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().total).to.equal(bru.getVar("managementOverdueTickets"));
  });

  test("a due date, when there is one, is in the past", function () {
    for (const row of res.getBody().items) {
      expect(row.ticketNumber).to.be.a("string");
      if (row.dueAt !== null) {
        expect(Date.parse(row.dueAt)).to.be.below(Date.now());
        expect(row.daysOverdue).to.be.at.least(0);
      } else {
        expect(row.daysOverdue).to.equal(null);
      }
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /management-dashboard/alerts/overdue-tickets — the Overdue Tickets drawer (PAC-139)

  The Service dashboard's tickets that have breached their SLA, opened in the
  window, oldest first. Each row opens `/crm/tickets?ticket=<ticketId>`.

  - **Module / permission / filter / paging:** as `List Stalled Leads`.
  - **Scope:** the CRM's own tenancy rule — `serviceTickets` stores its
    `agencyId`/`branchId` as ObjectIds — so a branch manager sees their branch
    and an `own`-scoped holder only tickets assigned to them.
  - **Person filter:** `producerIds` lands on `assignedUserId`, the CSR working
    the ticket. The filter bar lists every active user, so picking a service
    rep narrows this card the way picking a producer narrows the other two.
  - **`total`** equals the card's `overdueTickets` under the same query.

  ## What "overdue" is
  Partly derived. An onboarding or renewal call carries a scheduled step and is
  overdue when the step's `dueAt` has passed and it is not complete — whatever
  its stored `status` — unless a CSR pinned the status by hand. Every other
  ticket is overdue only when a CSR marked it so. The same predicate now feeds
  the Service dashboard's "needs action today" KPI, which used to read the
  stored field alone and missed every derived one.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "period": { "key": "ytd", "current": { "from": "2026-01-01", "to": "2026-09-23" }, "previous": { "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2025-09-23" } },
    "page": 1, "pageSize": 50, "total": 3, "totalPages": 1,
    "items": [
      {
        "ticketId": "66f0…e5", "ticketNumber": "BILL-103", "clientName": "Dana Whitfield",
        "category": "Billing", "assignedUserId": "66f0…22", "assignedRep": "Casey Kim",
        "householdId": "66f0…b2", "dueAt": null,
        "openedAt": "2026-09-13T14:02:11.000Z", "daysOverdue": null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  | field | notes |
  |---|---|
  | dueAt | the step's due instant; `null` for a hand-marked overdue ticket |
  | daysOverdue | whole days past `dueAt`; `null` when there is no due date to measure |

  ## Errors
  As `Get Alerts`.
}
